<section class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE IMPORTANT DETAILS</p><h1>Website terms.</h1><p class="page-lead">A few clear expectations for using this site.</p></section><section class="wrap legal-layout"><aside><span class="eyebrow">USING SHOPP.KE</span><a class="text-link" href="/reach-out">Need something clarified? <?= icon('arrow-up-right') ?></a></aside><div class="prose"><h2>About this website</h2><p>This website introduces Shopp.ke, its approach to independent selling, store setup, payments, and delivery. It provides information and a way to make enquiries or request a store.</p><h2>Store requests and enquiries</h2><p>Submitting a form is a request for a conversation. It does not create a seller account, activate a store, charge you, reserve delivery capacity, or start a paid subscription. Your on-screen reference confirms that the website saved your request.</p><h2>Plans, fees, and availability</h2><p>Plan descriptions introduce possible setups. Specific fees, service scope, payment arrangements, delivery routes, support, and commercial commitments must be confirmed in an applicable agreement before activation. A route enquiry is not a delivery booking.</p><h2>Seller field notes</h2><p>The seller articles are general editorial guides based on illustrative business scenarios. They are not verified customer testimonials, promises of results, financial advice, or guarantees of sales.</p><h2>Responsible use</h2><p>Provide information you are entitled to share. Do not submit unlawful content, impersonate another business, interfere with the site, or use forms for spam. Please keep passwords, payment credentials, and unnecessary sensitive information out of messages.</p><h2>Website content and links</h2><p>Do not present Shopp.ke branding or original content as your own. Third-party photography, fonts, and icons remain subject to their respective licences. External links lead to services we do not operate.</p><h2>Questions and future services</h2><p>Get in touch if anything here is unclear. Separate terms may apply to the seller application, payments, and delivery services; those details should be available before you commit.</p><a class="text-link" href="/reach-out">Let's clear it up <?= icon('arrow-up-right') ?></a></div></section>
